    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="67.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Af">Af</ref> 67.1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="67.1" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="84" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif hio<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="21" target="#Af_67-1.lnote.oe.21"/> bið onbestungen, geselle<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#Af_67-1.lnote.oe.12"/> XV<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="22" target="#Af_67-1.lnote.oe.22"/> scill. to<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="23" target="#Af_67-1.lnote.oe.23"/> bote.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="67.1" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="84" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif heo<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Af_67-1.lnote.oe.5"/> biþ onbestungen, gesylle XV scll' to bote.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="67.1" corresp="#wit-b-no-prol"><pb n="84" ed="#liebermann"/>Gyf héo bið onbestungen, fihtene<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_67-1.lnote.oe.2"/> scill'.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="67.1" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="85" ed="#liebermann"/>Si intus pungantur<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#Af_67-1.lnote.oe.13"/>, ad id faciunt XV sol.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="90" ed="#attenborough"/>Gif hio bið onbestungen, geselle XV scill. to bote.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="71.1" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="360" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>Gif hio bið unbestungen, geselle XV scill to bote.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="85" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenn sie eingestochen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_67-1.lnote.de.1"/> ist, gebe [der Thäter] 15 Schill. zur Busse.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If it is stabbed into, let [the offender] give 15 shillings as compensation.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="91" ed="#attenborough"/>If it is pierced, 15 shillings shall be given as compensation.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="361" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>If it is pierced into, let him pay 15 shillings as com- pensation.</ab>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_67-1.lnote.oe.21" n="21" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">84</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">heo <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">heo Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_67-1.lnote.oe.12" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">84</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_67-1.lnote.oe.22" n="22" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">84</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">fiftyne <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">fiftyne Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_67-1.lnote.oe.23" n="23" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">84</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">to b. <hi rend="italic">fehlt Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">to b. lacking in Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_67-1.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">84</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">eo <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">eo on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_67-1.lnote.oe.13" n="13" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">85</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">pungatur <hi rend="italic">T</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">pungatur T</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_67-1.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">84</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sic</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_67-1.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">62</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Vielleicht beeinflusst von Abt 64a. b übers Zeugungsglied, da auch hier Hinein- und Durchstechen und die entsprechenden Busssummen 6 und 12 Schill. vorkommen. In der Bibel, auch in <hi rend="italic">renes, lumbi</hi> der Vulgata, bezeichnen die Lenden den Sitz der Zeugungskraft. — Nicht ‘Rippenknochen’, da von Durchstechen die Rede ist, und Rippen <hi rend="italic">u.</hi> 70 vorkommen</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Perhaps influenced by Abt 64a. b on the genital member, since here too stabbing into and stabbing through occur, with the corresponding sums of compensation of 6 and 12 shill. In the Bible, including <hi rend="italic">renes, lumbi</hi> in the Vulgate, the loins denote the seat of the procreative power. — Not ‘rib-bones’, since stabbing through is spoken of, and ribs occur <hi rend="italic">below</hi> 70</seg></note>
      </div>
    </body>
